`git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short` also shows `lib/embedders/index.ts`, `lib/embedders/schema.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` and `scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. The first three predate my session. `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` changed **during** it — another wave-1 worker (T013's file), not my deriver: my regeneration run reported `changed: [".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json"]` only, and I hand-edited nothing but the two named files. `tests/command-metadata-e2e.vitest.ts` and `tests/doctor-command-bridges.vitest.ts` (the other two consumers of the generated file) both still pass, 7/7.

One cosmetic note, kept deliberately literal to the brief: joining with `. ` on descriptions that already end in `.` yields `.. `, and a removed leading slash command leaves a `. .` remnant in seven rows. Check 3 is unaffected (0). Say the word if you want a punctuation tidy in `commandEmbeddingText`.
